# Dive Schedule web — copy to .env.local for local dev. NEVER commit real env files.
# Base URL of the NestJS API that Next rewrites proxy /api/* and /webhooks/* to.
API_URL=http://localhost:4310

# Anti-clickjacking: origins allowed to frame the embedded app (space-separated), applied as a
# frame-ancestors CSP on the Next-served HTML. Defaults to the 'self' keyword (allows the same-origin
# dev harness). NOTE: for the 'self' keyword you must double-quote so dotenv keeps the inner single
# quotes (bare `self` is parsed as a hostname and blocks even same-origin framing). Real origins are
# plain URLs and need no quoting. Examples:
#   FRAME_ANCESTORS="'self'"
#   FRAME_ANCESTORS="https://app.eos.example https://app.your-vendor-domain.com"
# (Requires the app to be served by the Next Node runtime — `next start` — for headers() to apply.)

# The EOS workspace (host) origin the iframe bridge pins the identity token to / accepts messages from.
# The bridge NEVER posts to '*'. Unset in the same-origin dev harness (falls back to this app's own
# origin). NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime — set it in the build
# environment (or bake it into the build pipeline), e.g.:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_ORIGIN=https://app.eos.example
